+{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"reviewThreads":{"nodes":[{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eRky9","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_review.cljs","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908390861,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind lane results to their catalog actors**\n\nWhen candidate output is model-controlled or a producer is misconfigured, admission checks only that the claimed lane keyword is required; it never matches `:evidence/producer` or its revisions against that lane's catalog profile. Because `aggregate-verdict` receives no catalog at all, one arbitrary syntactically valid producer can claim every required lane and supply accepted blockers or complete results, defeating the dedicated-actor authority boundary. Validate each result against the selected lane profile before accepting it.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L9-L11](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/blob/847079d85578ccc7bc07543e40e8fdf8ca1b9f13/AGENTS.md#L9-L11)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/325#discussion_r3908390861"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eRky_","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_review.cljs","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908390865,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Match retained artifact references, not only hashes**\n\nWhen a finding reuses an inspected artifact's hash but supplies a different `:artifact/kind` or `:artifact/location`, this hash-only membership check admits it as retained. The fabricated reference can then support a confirmed blocker and appear in the aggregate even though that cited reference was never in the lane's inspected manifest; compare against the retained artifact references themselves or derive citation metadata from the manifest.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L9-L11](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/blob/847079d85578ccc7bc07543e40e8fdf8ca1b9f13/AGENTS.md#L9-L11)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/325#discussion_r3908390865"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eR1ri","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_review.cljs","line":102,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908493836,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject artifacts outside the selected lane's catalog**\n\nWhen an otherwise valid lane result places an arbitrary artifact kind in `:coverage/inspected` and cites that exact reference, admission never compares the artifact's kind with the resolved profile's `:lane/artifact-kinds`. A contracts/schema producer can therefore use test, CI, or fabricated artifact classes to support an accepted confirmed blocker, bypassing the catalog's dedicated evidence-class boundary; validate every inspected reference against the selected lane profile.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L9-L11](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/blob/8c27f2ddda691074e14982780a3f90922f804842/AGENTS.md#L9-L11)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/325#discussion_r3908493836"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eR1rq","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"packages/eta-mu/test/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_review_test.cljs","line":76,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908493847,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Pass an admissible catalog to verdict tests**\n\nEvery aggregation test passes the `required-lanes` set as argument two, but `aggregate-verdict` now requires a catalog and immediately runs `catalog-admissibility-errors` on it. The first test therefore throws `Invalid evidence lane catalog` before reaching any assertion, and the same mismatch affects every later call; update these tests and their lane-result fixtures to use the catalog-bound API.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L81-L83](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/blob/8c27f2ddda691074e14982780a3f90922f804842/AGENTS.md#L81-L83)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/325#discussion_r3908493847"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eR1r2","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"packages/eta-mu/test/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_lane_catalog_test.cljs","line":18,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908493860,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Read actor identities from the producer profile**\n\nThe catalog stores actors at `[:lane/producer :producer/actor]`, so mapping `:lane/actor` returns `[nil nil nil]` and this newly added uniqueness assertion always fails. The later shared-actor fixture uses the same obsolete path and consequently produces an invalid closed catalog rather than the expected shared-actor error; update both accesses to the nested producer field.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L81-L83](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/blob/8c27f2ddda691074e14982780a3f90922f804842/AGENTS.md#L81-L83)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/325#discussion_r3908493860"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eR1r8","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_review.cljs","line":128,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908493870,"author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"body":"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Enforce each lane's maximum finding budget**\n\nWhen a producer returns more findings than its catalog profile's `:max-findings`, this admission path only validates each finding individually and accepts the unbounded vector. That makes the advertised hard output bound non-enforcing and allows model-controlled results to exceed the 20/25-finding limits before aggregation; reject results whose finding count exceeds the selected lane budget.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L9-L11](https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/blob/8c27f2ddda691074e14982780a3f90922f804842/AGENTS.md#L9-L11)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/325#discussion_r3908493870"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORu27H86eR7j8","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_lane_catalog.cljs","line":85,"comments":{"nodes":[{"databaseId":3908529654,"author":{"login":"coderabbitai"},"body":"_🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\nset -e\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- scoped conventions ---'\nfind /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/open-hax-eta-mu-6e87152e -maxdepth 2 -type f -name '*.md' -print\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- applicable convention content ---'\nfor f in /tmp/coderabbit-repo-knowledge/open-hax-eta-mu-6e87152e/*/*.md; do\n  [ -f \"$f\" ] || continue\n  case \"$f\" in\n    *learnings*|*architecture*) continue ;;\n  esac\n  head -80 \"$f\"\ndone\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- target source ---'\ncat -n packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/domain/evidence_lane_catalog.cljs | sed -n '1,180p'\n```\n\nRepository: open-hax/eta-mu\n\nLength of output: 12607\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\nset -e\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- law namespace files ---'\nfd -t f 'evidence_lane_catalog|evidence-lane-catalog' packages\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- predicate and schema references ---'\nrg -n -C 8 'valid-catalog-shape|catalog.*shape|:catalog/lanes' packages/eta-mu/src packages/eta-mu/test packages/eta-mu/resources 2>/dev/null || true\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- package/runtime declarations -